            <ArticleTitle>Accidental veterinary antibiotic injection into a farm worker.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 29-year-old white male farm worker accidentally injected tilmicosin, a bovine antibiotic, into his finger. He developed temporary pulmonary, gastrointestinal, and neuromuscular symptomatology and a more persistent subjective asthenia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
